@startuml
title 1B - Discord: "/jardinero-code request:add retries to failed actions"\nThe command writes the ticket and hands it over; no routing agent runs

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor User
participant "DiscordAdapter" as DA
participant "Orchestrator" as O
participant "Store" as S
participant "LinearAdapter" as LA
participant Linear

User -> DA: /jardinero-code request:"..." [repo:...]
DA -> DA: resolve identity + repository
return actor, repo

alt the repository maps to exactly one Linear team
  DA -> Linear: create issue\ntitle = first line, description = the whole text
  return JAR-nn
  DA -> DA: open the Discord thread for JAR-nn
  DA -> O: create Request{subject=linear:JAR-nn, reply=thread}
  O -> S: create RequestRouter instance
  return rr_pending
  note right of O
    The subject is known, so the router resolves it without an
    agent: rr_pending sees subjectType set and goes straight to
    rr_resolved. No sandbox run is dispatched.
  end note

  DA -> Linear: delegate JAR-nn to Jardinero
  alt delegated
    Linear --> DA: ok
    O -> S: state
    return rr_resolved
    DA -> User: "Opened JAR-nn and started on it"
    note right of O
      The request machine ENDS here. It did not open the work.
      Work starts through the single door: the Linear webhook.
    end note
    Linear -> LA: AgentSessionEvent/created
    LA -> O: LinearRequest{subject=linear:JAR-nn}
    O -> S: create LinearImplementer instance
    return li_pending
    note right of O: continues exactly as 1A
  else Linear refused
    Linear --> DA: error
    O -> S: state
    return rr_unresolvable
    DA -> User: "Opened JAR-nn, but it could not be started.\nAsk again with /jardinero-ticket ticket:JAR-nn"
  end
else no team, or more than one
  DA -> User: refused, nothing is written
end
@enduml
